\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Two provisos travel with the table.
 The first is immutability.
 A mathematical object does not change:
 
\begin_inset Formula $\{1,2\}$
\end_inset

 is not a container whose contents may later differ,
 it is the set.
 Python distinguishes the two readings —
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
list
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
set
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
dict
\end_layout

\end_inset

 are mutable and therefore unhashable,
 while 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
tuple
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
frozenset
\end_layout

\end_inset

 are immutable and hashable —
 and only a hashable value may serve as an element of a 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
set
\end_layout

\end_inset

 or as a key of a 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
dict
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 Wherever the correspondence is read as an identification rather than as an implementation,
 the immutable member of the pair is the one meant.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The second is exactness.
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
int
\end_layout

\end_inset

 represents 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{Z}$
\end_inset

 faithfully and 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Fraction
\end_layout

\end_inset

 represents 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{Q}$
\end_inset

 faithfully,
 both to arbitrary precision.
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
float
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is not a representation of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

:
 it is a finite set of dyadic rationals,
 closed exactly under none of its own arithmetic,
 and 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
complex
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is a pair of those.
 Those two rows are approximations where the others are identifications,
 and every construction below is arranged so as not to need them.
\end_layout

