\begin_layout Subsection
Constants
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
An operation is rarely presented alone.
 For a binary 
\begin_inset Formula $\ast$
\end_inset

 on 
\begin_inset Formula $S$
\end_inset

,
 an element 
\begin_inset Formula $e$
\end_inset

 is an identity when 
\begin_inset Formula $e\ast a=a\ast e=a$
\end_inset

 for every 
\begin_inset Formula $a$
\end_inset

,
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $z$
\end_inset

 is absorbing when 
\begin_inset Formula $z\ast a=a\ast z=z$
\end_inset

;
 each is unique when it exists.
 Written as literals the familiar ones are short:
 
\begin_inset Formula $\top$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\bot$
\end_inset

 are 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
True
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
False
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 the additive and multiplicative units are 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
0
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
1
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 the empty set is 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
frozenset()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 and the unattainable end of an unbounded order is 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
math.inf
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
