\begin_layout Standard
Constants are not decoration,
 and 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "tab:constants"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset

 says why.
 Aggregating an operation over a family is a fold,
 and a fold over the empty family has nothing to combine,
 so it must return something chosen in advance;
 the only choice that keeps the fold consistent with itself is the identity,
 since adjoining an empty family to any other must leave the result alone.
 Python has already committed to this:
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
sum(())
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
0
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
math.prod(())
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
1
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
all(())
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
True
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
any(())
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
False
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 each of them the identity of the operation being folded and none of them a special case in the implementation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
min
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is the exception that states the rule.
 Taking a minimum is a meet,
 and its identity would be the greatest element of the order;
 but 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
min
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is defined over carriers that assume no such element,
 so the empty case has nothing to return and raises instead.
 Boundedness is exactly the hypothesis that makes finite aggregation total,
 which is why it is carried as part of the contract below rather than left to the caller.
\end_layout

